WEBVTT

00:03.190 --> 00:04.900
You've made your choice, I assume?

00:05.950 --> 00:06.710
Yes.

00:10.400 --> 00:13.670
The people are finally starting 
to get used to their new town.

00:14.590 --> 00:19.540
I told Cefiro-sama when I went 
to serve under her, but...

00:21.040 --> 00:26.140
my goal is a world where humans 
and demons can co-exist.

00:33.580 --> 00:36.140
I'm sorry, Demon Lord.

00:36.860 --> 00:42.100
I still have much to learn from Cefiro-sama.

00:45.840 --> 00:51.290
I'll make Ivalias the first town 
where humans and demons co-exist.

01:03.910 --> 01:06.870
There you are, Master.

01:07.100 --> 01:10.120
Is something bothering you?

01:10.120 --> 01:13.420
You've barely come inside 
since the duel ended.

01:14.480 --> 01:15.420
I knew it.

01:20.480 --> 01:22.520
With the soil and climate in this town,

01:23.280 --> 01:25.480
we can use the Norfolk system.

01:25.930 --> 01:26.780
Huh?

01:27.320 --> 01:32.440
It's a way to grow a lot of different 
crops without letting the fields rest.

01:32.910 --> 01:34.280
Um...

01:35.620 --> 01:40.240
Basically, you'll get to eat 
all the turnips you want.

01:40.580 --> 01:44.200
Really? I love turnips!

01:44.520 --> 01:45.690
Good.

01:46.320 --> 01:47.820
We're going to be busy soon.

01:51.860 --> 01:55.800
Busy making a town where humans 
and demons can live together.

03:53.500 --> 03:58.000
<i>Dwarf King</i>

04:06.640 --> 04:09.680
Is this the Norfolk system?

04:10.210 --> 04:14.160
Currently, we grow wheat, 
then let the field rest,

04:14.160 --> 04:19.950
then grow grass to feed livestock 
which we take our meat from, yes?

04:20.660 --> 04:21.700
Yes.

04:21.700 --> 04:25.580
But that means leaving the 
field fallow for a long time.

04:26.230 --> 04:32.870
Instead, we'll rotate between 
barley, clover, wheat, and turnips.

04:33.640 --> 04:36.250
That will allow us to grow crops 
without the need to let the fields rest.

04:38.530 --> 04:40.800
Can you eat clover?

04:41.300 --> 04:43.050
It's for livestock.

04:45.140 --> 04:50.510
If this works, neither humans 
nor demons will ever be hungry.

04:58.010 --> 05:00.520
Master, here.

05:00.800 --> 05:04.910
Oh, I heard you were 
promoted to vice-commander!

05:04.910 --> 05:06.240
Congratulations!

05:06.480 --> 05:07.680
Yes.

05:07.680 --> 05:10.410
There happened to be an 
opening for the position.

05:11.310 --> 05:14.660
I'll have to call you 
Vice-Commander from now on, huh?

05:14.660 --> 05:16.310
Ike-sama!

05:16.310 --> 05:17.880
T-Trouble!

05:18.800 --> 05:20.960
What's got you in such a rush?

05:20.960 --> 05:23.590
Well, you see, Ike-sama...

05:23.870 --> 05:25.290
Vice-Commander.

05:26.050 --> 05:27.800
I-I'm so sorry!

05:27.800 --> 05:32.720
You got a promotion and 
I'm still calling you by your name!

05:32.720 --> 05:35.770
I, Jiron, will accept any punishment.

05:37.150 --> 05:38.050
Oh, right!

05:38.050 --> 05:40.880
Is it true that you turned down 
an offer to be a corps commander?

05:40.880 --> 05:41.770
I never would...

05:41.770 --> 05:44.990
Didn't you have something 
important to tell me?

05:45.240 --> 05:45.960
Oh!

05:46.800 --> 05:48.320
What was it, again?

05:49.990 --> 05:51.780
Is it about the Alliance of Kings?

05:51.780 --> 05:54.000
Yes! That's right!

05:54.000 --> 05:55.800
They've finally started moving!

05:55.800 --> 05:57.130
Last night!

05:58.450 --> 06:02.380
The Second Corps, which was trying 
to take Alesta, was defeated!

06:03.410 --> 06:09.390
The Second Corps are a bloodthirsty 
bunch, but skilled warriors.

06:09.390 --> 06:12.760
I never thought they would lose so badly!

06:13.140 --> 06:16.960
It looks like calling the Alliance of
 Kings is already having an effect.

06:17.750 --> 06:20.860
Um, what's the Alliance of Kings?

06:20.860 --> 06:27.320
The Alliance of Kings is one of 
the humans' ancient treaties.

06:28.060 --> 06:33.570
When the power of the Demon Lord's army 
grows too strong for one nation to handle alone,

06:33.570 --> 06:37.290
the nations of the continent band 
together to do battle against them.

06:37.960 --> 06:40.790
Have there been alliance armies in the past?

06:41.240 --> 06:44.000
I'm told it happened 
three times in the past,

06:44.760 --> 06:47.970
and each time, 
the Demon Lord's army was defeated.

06:48.740 --> 06:50.760
Will we be okay?

06:51.100 --> 06:55.820
No. We here in Ivalias are 
probably their next target.

06:55.820 --> 06:57.950
R-Really?

06:59.100 --> 07:03.060
We took Arsenam, which is a critical base.

07:04.440 --> 07:07.080
And if they want to take it from us,

07:09.030 --> 07:13.070
they'll need to strike our 
front lines. Here, in Ivalias.

07:13.480 --> 07:16.720
Demons are more powerful one on one.

07:16.720 --> 07:20.970
But we'll struggle against their 
numbers and ability to work in unison.

07:22.290 --> 07:27.610
If Ivalias falls, the alliance army's 
forces will concentrate on Arsenam.

07:29.790 --> 07:35.680
They outnumber us, so if we're hit by a 
concentrated attack, we'll lose Arsenam.

07:36.720 --> 07:39.820
If that happens, the Demon Lord's 
army will be forced

07:39.820 --> 07:42.470
to fall back to Doberberg, 
where the Demon Lord's castle is.

07:42.470 --> 07:44.950
We'll be in dire straits.

07:44.950 --> 07:47.440
Th-That's really bad!

07:48.010 --> 07:52.590
<i>And my dream of making a town where humans 
and demons co-exist will disappear as well.</i>

07:55.150 --> 08:00.410
There's only one way to overcome 
their overwhelming numbers.

08:00.810 --> 08:01.930
One way?

08:03.250 --> 08:08.550
So what we found is that constructing 
these firearms with alchemy is impossible.

08:09.040 --> 08:10.580
And why?

08:10.580 --> 08:14.010
We made several similar ones,

08:15.720 --> 08:19.260
but they break after firing one bullet.

08:23.440 --> 08:28.890
There's a limit to the degree of 
precision you can get with alchemy.

08:28.890 --> 08:32.280
Their penetrating power and durability 
will only be that of a copy.

08:32.720 --> 08:35.490
Yes. They're weak, as well.

08:35.930 --> 08:39.260
Do we even need these?

08:39.260 --> 08:41.440
Can't we just flatten them with magic?

08:41.440 --> 08:45.040
Mass destruction makes
 it hard to rebuild!

08:45.040 --> 08:46.710
I know that!

08:46.710 --> 08:49.490
If we're going to fight the alliance,

08:49.490 --> 08:51.800
we need weapons anyone can use.

08:52.690 --> 08:55.030
It will be difficult to mass-produce them,

08:55.030 --> 08:57.180
but one way we could do it would be

08:57.560 --> 09:02.800
to make the parts that are made 
of metal and wood one by one.

09:02.800 --> 09:06.010
How would you make something so small?

09:06.010 --> 09:07.990
Especially the ones made of metal.

09:07.990 --> 09:10.900
What about a race that is 
highly skilled in metalwork?

09:11.990 --> 09:14.220
You mean the dwarves.

09:15.150 --> 09:18.940
Well, the dwarves might 
be able to make them.

09:19.420 --> 09:20.490
But...

09:21.560 --> 09:27.740
They lost their battle with the humans and 
are now a lost people wandering the lands.

09:28.890 --> 09:32.690
We'll need a lot of dwarves to mass-produce
 the number of weapons we'll need.

09:33.250 --> 09:36.050
How will you bring them together?

09:37.190 --> 09:38.760
Well...

09:39.380 --> 09:40.970
The Dwarf King.

09:41.890 --> 09:46.330
The king held captive in Ismuth Kingdom.

09:53.430 --> 09:57.450
You should've just done what you were told.

09:57.870 --> 10:01.160
Then this wouldn't have happened.

10:02.980 --> 10:05.580
You made us do extra work.

10:05.580 --> 10:10.790
Shut up! I won't let you humans 
use our technology for your wars!

10:16.570 --> 10:18.970
You're not listening at all, huh?

10:19.510 --> 10:22.430
Maybe you still don't 
understand the situation.

10:22.430 --> 10:24.930
You don't have a choice.

10:26.090 --> 10:27.090
Father!

10:31.210 --> 10:33.570
I won't let you hurt Batson!

10:34.670 --> 10:37.850
This is your last chance.

10:37.850 --> 10:42.480
You dwarves must use your power for Ismuth.

10:42.480 --> 10:46.760
If you do, we'll let you live.

10:54.910 --> 10:57.630
<i>Batson... Everyone...</i>

10:58.730 --> 11:01.070
<i>What are you all doing now?</i>

11:15.170 --> 11:16.740
I finally found you!

11:16.740 --> 11:17.780
A demon?

11:22.810 --> 11:25.010
Come on, let's go.

11:25.010 --> 11:27.140
What would a demon want with me?

11:27.140 --> 11:29.710
Just come with me, okay?

11:29.710 --> 11:33.670
But why would a demon want to save me?

11:34.070 --> 11:38.470
Will an old man like this 
really be useful to Ike-sama?

11:39.820 --> 11:41.840
Can't you hear me?

11:41.840 --> 11:43.280
Why would a demon...

11:43.280 --> 11:44.340
Enough!

11:54.060 --> 11:56.180
What did you do?

11:56.180 --> 12:01.270
Well, I got sick of all his questions.

12:02.410 --> 12:05.160
Come on. Let's get him out of here.

12:06.170 --> 12:09.920
Sheesh. That's the Dwarf King, you know.

12:14.790 --> 12:16.040
Creepy.

12:23.720 --> 12:25.760
Okay, nobody's here.

12:27.340 --> 12:30.080
I'm bored since there's no guards.

12:30.080 --> 12:33.270
We were told not to let 
anybody see us taking him.

12:33.270 --> 12:34.480
Shut up and move!

12:37.710 --> 12:39.010
What's wrong?

12:39.010 --> 12:41.020
You smell weird.

12:41.020 --> 12:42.900
Like how?

12:42.900 --> 12:45.360
You smell ugly!

12:45.360 --> 12:47.990
Do you want to get killed here?

12:47.990 --> 12:50.970
I just told the truth.

12:50.970 --> 12:52.060
Hey, who's there?

12:52.940 --> 12:54.290
D-Demons!

12:55.360 --> 12:57.900
We were discovered because of you!

12:57.900 --> 12:58.750
Oh, my.

12:58.750 --> 13:00.210
Capture them!

13:00.620 --> 13:03.670
They look nice and lively.

13:06.380 --> 13:08.570
I'll make a nice meal out of them!

13:09.610 --> 13:13.060
The vice-commander told you not to get 
into fights if you could avoid it!

13:13.310 --> 13:15.440
Oh, did he?

13:15.440 --> 13:17.690
Oh, is that your answer?

13:18.200 --> 13:20.710
I'll tell him all about this.

13:21.650 --> 13:23.840
Stop, monsters!

13:25.230 --> 13:27.240
Die!

13:30.580 --> 13:32.740
Oh, drat!

13:32.740 --> 13:36.560
Weren't you supposed to avoid fights?

13:36.560 --> 13:38.730
I'll tell Ike-sama!

13:39.550 --> 13:41.760
Please! Don't!

13:41.760 --> 13:43.300
I'm gonna!

13:43.580 --> 13:47.010
I've got my position as his 
strategist to think about!

13:47.320 --> 13:51.220
Then stop oinking like a pig all the time.

13:51.220 --> 13:53.870
I do not oink!

13:53.870 --> 13:56.820
Oh, you don't realize?

14:06.750 --> 14:07.660
Oink?

14:08.410 --> 14:11.030
I told you to stop...

14:11.330 --> 14:12.800
Demons!

14:12.800 --> 14:14.790
Demons are inside the walls!

14:15.210 --> 14:17.790
Damn it! Why are they all here?

14:17.790 --> 14:19.460
Hey, do something!

14:19.460 --> 14:20.750
Fine.

14:27.850 --> 14:29.180
What?

14:29.540 --> 14:34.910
I promised Ike-sama... so I won't kill you.

14:39.080 --> 14:41.830
I told them to avoid detection.

14:41.830 --> 14:44.560
They're attracting a lot of attention.

14:45.310 --> 14:50.670
Why are there so many soldiers? 
I thought the Alliance took them all!

14:50.670 --> 14:54.620
Yeah. I'm full, too.

14:54.620 --> 14:56.310
Don't let them get away!

15:00.860 --> 15:02.040
What are those?

15:05.500 --> 15:07.280
Good work, both of you.

15:08.630 --> 15:10.010
Ike-sama!

15:10.460 --> 15:13.360
That was you, right?

15:13.360 --> 15:15.210
How wonderful.

15:15.210 --> 15:16.210
Sheesh...

15:16.210 --> 15:19.000
Why don't you give me a welcome back kiss?

15:19.000 --> 15:20.020
Were there any issues?

15:21.250 --> 15:23.610
None! None at all!

15:23.610 --> 15:26.190
We've got the Dwarf King!

15:26.190 --> 15:29.900
Look, he's the king.
You can't carry him like that.

15:29.900 --> 15:32.700
I'm sorry!

15:32.700 --> 15:35.600
Wake up, Dwarf King!

15:35.600 --> 15:38.720
I just said be a little more gentle with him!

15:55.360 --> 15:56.850
Are you awake?

15:58.840 --> 16:01.560
Gunther-sama, King of the Dwarves.

16:02.520 --> 16:04.240
Demons?

16:04.240 --> 16:07.580
Why did you take me out of my cell?

16:07.580 --> 16:09.610
Tell me.

16:15.180 --> 16:17.440
Can you make another one of these?

16:18.920 --> 16:21.000
I've never seen one of these before.

16:21.000 --> 16:24.200
It looks simple at first glance,
 but it's actually quite complex.

16:24.200 --> 16:27.670
It will take time, but I can do it.

16:28.650 --> 16:29.360
Then...

16:29.360 --> 16:33.260
But why must I work for demons?

16:33.780 --> 16:37.380
I refuse to help you.

16:38.860 --> 16:44.250
You intend to use us, just like the humans.

16:45.320 --> 16:51.140
You can take my life, 
but I'll never be your slave!

16:51.140 --> 16:54.200
It's only natural that you'd think that way.

16:55.410 --> 16:58.530
But this is needed for 
the sake of my ideals.

16:58.530 --> 17:02.550
No, for peace between humans and demons.

17:02.550 --> 17:04.210
What are you talking about?

17:04.210 --> 17:06.170
Follow me, please.

17:13.910 --> 17:15.440
What's this?

17:15.440 --> 17:19.970
I want demons and humans to live in peace.

17:20.670 --> 17:23.600
And I want your help.

17:25.610 --> 17:27.600
That's interesting.

17:27.600 --> 17:30.770
But I can't understand it.

17:31.660 --> 17:39.780
The humans used us dwarves, 
and then destroyed our country.

17:39.780 --> 17:45.410
And now we're forced to wander the land.

17:45.830 --> 17:51.040
Why do I have to help you, if it helps them?

17:51.630 --> 17:54.840
I don't care if they live in peace.

17:54.840 --> 18:00.310
What if we could bring 
back the peace you had?

18:00.310 --> 18:01.470
What?

18:01.900 --> 18:04.670
If you'll mass-produce the firearms,

18:04.670 --> 18:09.690
I'll ask the Demon Lord to 
rebuild the Dwarf Kingdom.

18:10.540 --> 18:12.570
Are you mocking me?

18:12.570 --> 18:13.900
If this is a joke, then stop!

18:14.310 --> 18:17.320
It's not that easy to rebuild a nation!

18:17.320 --> 18:20.610
You can't rebuild a nation 
without its people!

18:20.610 --> 18:26.000
I've lost my people! My family!

18:26.450 --> 18:29.990
See for yourself if it's a joke.

18:51.540 --> 18:52.410
Father!

18:52.410 --> 18:53.690
Gunther-sama!

18:53.690 --> 18:56.820
Batson! And all of you!

18:56.820 --> 18:58.160
How?

18:58.640 --> 19:01.050
The demons suddenly brought us here!

19:01.050 --> 19:02.830
We thought we were doomed, but...

19:02.830 --> 19:05.590
They gave us food and a place to live,

19:05.590 --> 19:07.290
and brought us all together again!

19:08.080 --> 19:10.950
You really saved the king!

19:10.950 --> 19:11.650
Indeed.

19:11.650 --> 19:13.250
So that's it...

19:13.690 --> 19:19.340
All right, everyone! For the king's sake, 
let's show them what we dwarves can do.

19:19.600 --> 19:22.000
Yeah!

19:22.000 --> 19:23.510
I'll ask again.

19:24.490 --> 19:27.090
Will you help me with my ambition?

19:27.760 --> 19:28.980
Very well.

19:28.980 --> 19:33.690
I've decided I want to see 
this "ambition" of yours.

19:46.770 --> 19:50.710
<i>For a demon, he has warm hands.</i>

19:59.410 --> 20:03.640
Welcome back. I'll prepare tea.

20:05.890 --> 20:08.100
Why don't you get some rest?

20:08.450 --> 20:13.280
No, it's easier to distract 
myself if I do something.

20:13.280 --> 20:16.810
If you like books, you can read 
them when you're not working.

20:16.810 --> 20:20.920
Oh, well I like looking at them...

20:20.920 --> 20:23.570
But I can't read.

20:24.710 --> 20:25.940
I see.

20:26.620 --> 20:29.540
I'll teach you when I have free time, then.

20:29.540 --> 20:31.170
Really?

20:31.170 --> 20:32.500
That makes me so happy!

20:36.850 --> 20:41.170
I brought back all the dwarves 
scattered across Arsenam!

20:42.660 --> 20:44.380
E-Excellent!

20:45.820 --> 20:49.100
You're trying to seduce my 
Ike-sama again, aren't you?

20:51.680 --> 20:55.560
I was just doing some work for my master.

20:56.860 --> 20:58.880
You're getting cocky, aren't you?

21:04.590 --> 21:05.830
Both of you...

21:05.830 --> 21:10.090
Vice-Commander! Trouble!

21:11.710 --> 21:13.410
Shut up! Ugly pig!

21:13.810 --> 21:16.870
Oink! Did I do something wrong?

21:21.250 --> 21:25.880
General, the Dwarf King 
was taken by the Demons.

21:28.130 --> 21:31.260
I don't know what the demons are thinking,

21:31.260 --> 21:33.730
but what could that old man even do?

21:35.750 --> 21:37.420
I've returned!

21:37.420 --> 21:40.120
How many forces do they have at Ivalias?

21:40.120 --> 21:41.740
Five hundred at the moment.

21:41.740 --> 21:46.200
All the brigade commanders are heading 
to support them, so it should increase.

21:46.870 --> 21:50.160
And how many do we have?

21:50.770 --> 21:53.120
Twelve battalions...

21:53.440 --> 21:55.330
So 12,000 men.

21:58.960 --> 22:01.730
Now, time to go.

23:34.140 --> 23:38.890
<i>War Begins</i>
